{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Moses stripped Aaron of his garments.</b> The garments of the high priesthood — he stripped them and put them on Eleazar in his presence. And now Moses took what was his and the Holy One, blessed be He, took what was His: Moses stripped them from him and took what he had given him — for he was the one who clothed him with them when he was inducted into the high priesthood, as it says (Leviticus 8:7), ״וילבש משה את אהרן את בגדיו״ — 'And Moses clothed Aaron with his garments'; and afterward the Holy One, blessed be He, took what He had given him, for thus our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: Moses said to him, 'Enter the cave,' and he entered; he saw a bed spread and a lamp burning. He said to him, 'Go up onto the bed,' and he went up; 'Stretch out your hands,' and he stretched them out; 'Open your mouth,' and he opened it; 'Close your eyes,' and he closed them. Immediately Moses longed for that death, and this is what was said to him (Deuteronomy 32:50): ״כאשר מת אהרן אחיך״ — 'as Aaron your brother died' — in that very death which he had longed for. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in Torat Kohanim: an act of miracles was performed with these garments. Now surely the lower ones are always lower and the upper ones always upper; rather, the Place (i.e., HaShem) performed an act of miracles for Aaron at his death more than in his lifetime, for Moses stripped them from him in their proper order. And so we find that Scripture uses identical language for the clothing and the stripping: for the clothing it says (Leviticus 8:7), ״וילבש משה את אהרן את בגדיו״, and likewise for the stripping, ״ויפשט משה את אהרן את בגדיו״ — that is, 'he stripped' in the same sense as 'he clothed.'" "<b>And know</b> that the place, which is Mount Hor, was to the south, and it was fitting that Aaron be buried there, for the measure of the right side is his measure; and Miriam was in Kadesh, which is between north and south; and Moses on Mount Nebo, which is between them. And a person can pass from there to each and every grave; therefore it is called 'Mount ha-Avarim' (the mountain of passes), for it is open to both sides. And therefore the brothers were not buried in one place, so that each would be in the place fitting for him, and also so as to protect Israel and atone for them in those places where they were prone to sin. And the fact that the gathering of Aaron was juxtaposed to the pericope of the king of Edom — they said in the Midrash: this is what Scripture says (II Chronicles 20:37), ״בהתחברך לרשע פרץ ה' את מעשיך״ — 'Because you joined yourself with the wicked, HaShem has broken your works' — because they joined with this wicked one to cross his border, they lost that righteous man." "<b>And Aaron died there on the summit of the mountain.</b> And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: three died by the kiss — Moses, Aaron, and Miriam. Regarding Moses and Aaron it says concerning them 'על פי HaShem' ('by the mouth of HaShem'), but regarding Miriam it does not say 'על פי HaShem,' because it would be unseemly to say so of a woman." "<b>And one may wonder</b> that we do not find here that Scripture mentioned in connection with Aaron's death on the summit of the mountain 'על פי HaShem' ('by the mouth of HaShem'), as it said regarding Moses (Deuteronomy 34:5): ״וימת שם משה עבד ה' בארץ מואב על פי ה'״ — 'And Moses the servant of HaShem died there in the land of Moab, by the mouth of HaShem.' He did not wish to mention this concerning him in this place, because in this place they rebelled against the mouth of HaShem in the sin of striking the rock twice, as was explained above. And how could it be that Scripture would mention in this place that his death was through the very One whom they rebelled against — namely, 'the mouth of HaShem,' concerning which it is written ״על אשר מריתם את פי״ ('because you rebelled against My mouth')? And because it was not mentioned here, it was necessary to mention it elsewhere, in the pericope of Eleh Massei, which is what he explained there (Numbers 33:38): ״ויעל אהרן הכהן אל הר ההר על פי ה' וימת שם״ — 'And Aaron the priest went up to Mount Hor by the mouth of HaShem, and died there.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:36.907903278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}